# The Zenodo concept DOI is added under `identifiers:` once the first GitHub
# release mints it. Version and date-released are finalised at release time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
title: "bulk-rna-preprocessing: a reusable Salmon-quant to h5ad preprocessing stage for bulk RNA-seq"
abstract: >-
  A small, reusable Snakemake workflow that aggregates a tree of per-sample Salmon
  quantifications into gene- and transcript-level AnnData (.h5ad) objects with
  upper-quartile (UQN / log2_uqn) normalisation layers, an obs sample/clinical
  join, and GENCODE + HGNC var annotation (gene_name, gene_type, hgnc_id,
  entrez_id). It is the bulk-RNA analogue of chromium-preprocessing: a
  config-driven, containerisable stage that runs standalone or as a git submodule
  within a DVC-tracked dataset. It is assay/subtyper-agnostic — downstream PAM50
  intrinsic subtyping (intrinsix) self-identifies its genes from var.entrez_id, so
  no classifier-specific columns are stamped here.
type: software
